  "notes": "USAGE:\nA compound verb formed from {追|お}う (to chase) + かける (to begin/to do toward). More colloquial than {追|お}う alone, and emphasizes the active motion of running after something.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {犬|いぬ}が{追|お}いかける (a dog chases)\n- {夢|ゆめ}を{追|お}いかける (to pursue a dream)\n- {流行|りゅうこう}を{追|お}いかける (to chase trends)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {追|お}う: to chase, to pursue — more general and also used in written language\n- {追跡|ついせき}する: to track, to pursue — more formal, used for investigations or surveillance",
